From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:17:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HID: dockchannel: freeze interface creation across system
 sleep

The transport now notifies HID drivers across suspend and resume, with
suspend rollback and all-interface resume error handling. Keep those
callbacks and make the interface creation workqueue freezable so no HID
device is added, or dropped after failed registration, while they walk
the interfaces.

This carries the remaining transport change from the click-strength
resume series; the newer sleep notifications already provide its
hid_driver_resume() calls.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>

(backported from commit aa00d6703a8a27df8311b9e3202c3c3c997e954d)
[j604: context only: the 1.607 probe has no receive-ring allocation before the
 workqueue (Aurora d8b19e08ab is not in this tree); the one-line change is the same.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c b/drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c
index c09e4e9f67..995af35d8e 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c
@@ -1454,7 +1454,11 @@ static int dockchannel_hid_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		dev_warn(dev, "Failed to set up wakeup: %d\n", ret);
 
-	dchid->new_iface_wq = alloc_ordered_workqueue("dchid-new", 0);
+	/*
+	 * Freeze interface creation across system sleep so the HID devices
+	 * stay stable while the suspend and resume callbacks walk them.
+	 */
+	dchid->new_iface_wq = alloc_ordered_workqueue("dchid-new", WQ_FREEZABLE);
 	if (!dchid->new_iface_wq)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
